Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayGraphics3D", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"a55e786f-6e45-7044-ab6a-4fdd7968dee5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"711a6bb6-9885-1347-8882-4bdf4b0eab8c"],
 " ",
 "draws the array arr as cubes arranged in space."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d323f93f-3c3f-c64e-88c5-80aafbc39bd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr", ",", " ", "opts"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7ac46dac-5ff3-ce40-8d8a-82940b5a2a8a"],
 " ",
 "draws it with the given options."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"22fd22a7-634c-5f43-8d53-1d588c206b49"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"68681559-6284-ee4c-bf99-9d06a2de6bf6"],

Cell["\<\
An array of order one is drawn as a line of cubes, one of order two as a \
plane of them, and one of order three as a lattice. The entry at index tuple \
(i, j, k) sits at the point {i, j, k}, an index the array does not have \
standing at one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a6e3fc27-45ab-c743-b038-c46424476292"],

Cell["\<\
An array of higher order is drawn by tiling: the inner block of indices is \
drawn as a lattice, and the outer block repeats that lattice through space, \
shifted by its own extent and a gap. Everything ends up in one picture, since \
space has no room for pictures inset into pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"57d73bbb-ea8e-5549-b10c-b2a3225a4c17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is always a three-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Graphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e1408122-9ebb-6c49-a598-788db8899d52"],
 ". For plane pictures at every order see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cc9f9ddc-b513-1147-94e2-468449fdc962"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c58b7125-4d31-d243-aa71-a7cae77bbb17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Nesting\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k1", ",", " ", "k2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ec456ac9-7dca-5046-8350-f985c4f094dd"],
 " says how to split the indices: the blocks must sum to the order of the \
array and each must be one, two or three, space holding no more at a time. \
The default uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayNesting", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c706df7d-a3ba-424d-b6f0-bc483732ea5b"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"12b94d48-04da-914c-ac76-c52ccb7d5e8d"],

Cell["\<\
The cubes have translucent faces and no outline, so that the entries behind \
them can still be read; an outline on every cube of a lattice reads as a mesh \
rather than as a set of cells.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"199a32e7-4453-914c-bd89-8f9d43fac36a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A gnomon in the near corner marks as many axes as the picture uses; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Gnomon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5fdf6a9f-2b78-fe41-ab12-503b54af66c6"],
 " drops it. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Indices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Colored\>\""}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a9f606b2-f456-9b4e-b3e5-c4a81571fd67"],
 " gives each axis a colour of its own."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f67b57d-a025-024e-afdb-774b66aeeb49"],

Cell["\<\
The reference implementation this package grew out of drew only the \
order-three case, and called such a picture a cubix; the name is not kept, \
but the look of it is.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d1cf66be-31bf-624e-9fdb-923398d423dc"],

Cell["The other options are shared with ArrayGraphics.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6a483b10-cc4b-b547-8466-c27634ee5b32"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"96c47160-b072-2644-a7da-110739634283"],

Cell["At order one a line of cubes, at order two a plane of them:", \
"ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"aad6a397-6467-d94b-8a22-f03d309bc746"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics3D[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics3D[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"47c60bc7-af5e-8a43-9d68-a321bcd786e4"],

